    THE OBVIOUS ONE. Printed 174 restricts Espionage to disguise, sniper,
    tracking and wilderness survival, and prints "Wilderness: None" four lines
    later. Wilderness Survival is a WILDERNESS-category skill in this catalog,
    and a cross-category `only` is admitted solely when the class also lists
    that skill''s real category - so transcribing both lines literally made the
    skill granted and NOT TAKEABLE, which class-check reports as `unreachable`.
    Caught by the check, not by reading. Resolved by listing Wilderness with
    `only: ["Wilderness Survival"]` at the Espionage line''s +10%: the player can
    take that one skill and no other Wilderness skill, which is what the two
    lines mean together. "Wilderness: None" is the general rule and the
    Espionage line is its stated exception.
  - Science is printed as None and is therefore absent from occ_related_skills
    rather than listed empty. Wilderness is present for the reason above.
  - Six issued items are choices the book does not resolve or have no catalog
    row, and none is stubbed: a choice of T-10 or T-12 body armour, an automatic
    pistol of choice, an energy pistol of choice, an energy rifle of choice, a
    gun holster of choice, and two pairs of handcuffs. The billy club/riot club
    (1D6 S.D.C.) and the two tear gas grenades have no rows either. In the body.
  - The X-60 Flanker and the hovercycle or hover pod issued alongside are NOT
    stored: the Flanker is a BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3 vessel, as are the T-11
    Enhanced body armour, X-10A Predator and X-535 Jager offered on assignment.
    In the body.
  - starting_money is the first-level savings the book prints, 1D4x1000 - the
    lowest in the book, shared with the NGR Infantry Soldier it shares a ladder
    with. The 2500 credit monthly salary and the 4000 a month for 9th level and
    higher are pay rather than starting coin and are in the body.
  - Skill bases are catalog base plus the printed bonus, already added.
