## Lore

The New German Republic''s law enforcement officer. Police, whether on civilian or military duty, coordinate all operations with the military and use military personnel. Training covers investigation, streetwise, urban combat, and piloting the X-60 Flanker, X-10A Predator and X-535 Jager power armour.

Most NGR police are honest, caring and well intentioned, and many try to give D-bees a fair hearing. About 25% believe in human supremacy and treat all D-bees as suspects, bending rules and using unnecessary force; those officers can be unprincipled, anarchist or aberrant. About 8% are genuinely corrupt - taking bribes, stealing, working with criminals, arms dealers or the enemy, and dealing in extortion, assassination, destruction of evidence and forgery.

Alignment: Any.

## Jurisdiction

Civilian and urban crime falls to the local or federal courts, and justice inside the NGR is usually quick and fair. The level of technology means many perpetrators are heavily armed, or are borgs, juicers, crazies, or punks high on augmenting drugs or clad in power armour.

Supernatural monsters, enemy soldiers, conspirators and D-bees are enemies of the State and fall entirely to the military, which tracks, captures, interrogates, sentences and punishes them - trials may not apply. Police duties therefore include hunting down supernatural predators, invading monsters and marauding entities, and learning to recognise possession, mind control, illusions and shape-changing. Deadly force is considered reasonable, and a non-human who does not surrender at once is likely to be shot; even one who does surrender is likely to be restrained roughly and treated badly, with no apology or recompense if later found innocent.

## Rank and pay

Law Enforcement Officers share the military rank and command structure, but the lowest rank given to an LEO is corporal; the most common are sergeant, lieutenant, detective lieutenant and captain. Salary is 2500 credits a month, rising to 4000 for ninth level and higher, with a small four room apartment near the station and free meals at station cafeterias or military bases. Weapons, ammunition, vehicles and equipment are provided by the military.

## Cybernetics

None to start. Any augmentation must be purchased or given as a reward for heroism.

## GM Notes

Issued alongside the stored equipment, and not given catalog rows: a choice of T-10 or T-12 body armour (the T-12 in light grey with no medic symbols), an automatic pistol of choice - typically 9 or 10 mm - an energy pistol of choice, an energy rifle of choice - typically the TX-42 or TX-16 pump rifle - a gun holster of choice, two pairs of handcuffs, a billy club or riot club doing 1D6 S.D.C., and two tear gas grenades. Also the X-60 Flanker and a hovercycle or hover pod, which are vessel-shaped stat blocks this catalog does not hold.

Available on assignment: additional weapons, energy clips and vehicles, T-40 plain clothes body armour, T-11 Enhanced body armour, the X-10A Predator, the X-535 Jager, a medical kit, portable computer, cameras, surveillance equipment and basic supplies, plus access to police stations and their stores, police computers and databases, low-clearance military computers, and local jails and prisons. Provided on an as-needed basis.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ngr-police');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ngr-police';

